    "# Raven Poof Intro\n\nAn intro for your video: your figurine or object bursts into a flock of ravens that fly off, then your title appears over the empty shelf. The clip is matched to your photo's exposure, with a whoosh on the burst. 9:16.\n\nFreeField preset `raven-intro`. Runs on an 8 GB GPU. Open weights only.\n\n## Fill in\n- A photo of a figurine or object on a shelf or table: the node **Your photo (preset input)**\n- Title (e.g. your channel name): typed in the FreeField app (`--caption` on the command line)\n\n## Stages, left to right\n- 1\\. Your photo\n- 2\\. Animate (Wan 2.2 TI2V-5B)\n- Save\n\n## Models\n- `Wan2_2-TI2V-5B-Turbo-Q6_K.gguf`\n- `umt5-xxl-encoder-Q5_K_M.gguf`\n- `wan2.2_vae.safetensors`\n\n## What happens\nThis graph is Raven Poof. FreeField's `freefield/raven_intro.py` checks the frame edges, re-renders a take with a stray hand, matches the exposure to your photo and adds your title and a whoosh.\n\n## Run it\n1. Pick your file in the input node above and press Run.\n\nOr run the whole effect in FreeField: `python -m freefield run raven-intro --photo me.jpg`\n\nLicense: Apache-2.0 weights (Wan 2.2 TI2V-5B); exposure match, title and whoosh by FreeField\n"
   ],
